{"type":"npc","name":"Tanbogami","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":240,"temp":0,"max":240,"details":""},"ac":{"value":32,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":40,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":40}],"details":" water walk"},"weaknesses":[{"type":"cold-iron","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"fire","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","spirituan","thalassic"],"details":"Telepathy 100 feet"},"level":{"value":12},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Tanbogamis are kami warriors who protect rice fields and work with farmers to help bring a bountiful harvest. Tanbogamis have an impressive command over the amount of rainfall a field receives, with floods and droughts being the signs of a tanbogami's displeasure. Though given their role as protectors and cultivators, tanbogami are more hospitable to mortals than most kami.</p><p>Farmers often perform ritual ceremonies in devotion to the tanbogami at the beginning of the year and during harvest time. They also pray to the tanbogami in case of disaster or a poor harvest. During these ceremonies, the local tanbogami often reveal themselves to bless the fields, purify crops, and manage the amount of rainfall. In the direst of circumstances, a tanbogami can create vast yields of rice for starving villages.</p><h2>Limits of the Domain</h2><p>A tanbogami can wander far afield from its chosen community, patrolling the wilderness and even visiting neighboring settlements. However, they can't set foot in a rice field that belongs to a different settlement than their own. An evildoer or an evil spirit that flees to a neighboring rice field can use it as a sanctuary, remaining safe from the tanbogami for as long as they remain there.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 250/560/1,030 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing, slashing), armor (light), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Lore [Farming], Nature, Religion, Stealth, Survival)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, dexterity, elongating, energy resistant (fire, vitality), holy, ice, sensory (darkvision), spells (Divine: @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.qXTB7Ec9yYh5JPPV]{Cleanse Cuisine}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e-anachronism.spells.zfn5RqAdF63neqpP]{Control Water}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.Mt6ZzkVX8Q4xigFq]{Create Food}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e-anachronism.spells.K4LXpaBWrGy6jIER]{Downpour}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.Seaah9amXg70RKw2]{Water Walk}), spiked, spirit, strength, throwing, water, wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Benjamin Sulzer","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":7},"dex":{"mod":6},"con":{"mod":5},"int":{"mod":2},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":3}},"perception":{"details":"rain sight","mod":22,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"wavesense","acuity":"imprecise","range":100}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":22,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":25,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":19,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":24},"athletics":{"base":25},"nature":{"base":22},"religion":{"base":22},"stealth":{"base":23},"survival":{"base":22}},"traits":{"value":["holy","kami","spirit","water"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"lg"}}},"_id":"kVnAJHIGESI6fDHr","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/tanbogami.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tanbogami","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":2,"height":2,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/tanbogami.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"rotation":0,"t